The area of one of these triangles (for example, $\triangle PRQ$) is $\frac{1}{4}$ of the area of the square, or $1\mbox{ cm}^2.$ So the area of quadrilateral $DRQC$ is therefore $12.5-1=\boxed{11.5}\mbox{ cm}^2.$

